  {"comment": "An adjustment layer is one row, and filters attached to it are listed under it. The default arrangement at 1920 by 1080, two orange strokes on Layer 1. Levels is made as a filter layer through the layer kind browser and its window is applied: the list shows one Levels row and no record under it (shot 1). A real double click on that row's picture opens Levels' settings, a single press opening nothing (shot 2) and Cancel puts the window away. Curves is attached to the layer and is listed under its row (shot 3). One undo takes Curves off and the layer is still one row (shot 4), one redo brings it back. The document is saved and opened again and the list is the same (shot 5)."},
